# ContextStream (when MCP is enabled)

**Tool names:** Use the exact names your MCP client exposes. Session bootstrap: call **init** (session_init) then **context** (context_smart). Docs may say session_init/context_smart; the server often exposes **init** and **context**.

When the ContextStream MCP server is available:

- **Session bootstrap (mandatory—no exceptions):** On the **first message** of every new conversation, your **very first action** must be: (1) **init**(folder_path=<repo root>, context_hint=<user's message or "WinPodiums Phase 1 MVP">) then (2) **context**(user_message=<user's message>, format=minified, max_tokens=400). On **every subsequent message**, call **context**(user_message=<current message>, format=minified, max_tokens=400) at the start of your turn—do not skip. Use max_tokens=800 only for complex queries. If ContextStream MCP is unavailable or returns an error, **fall back immediately** to [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [docs/architecture/next-steps.md](../../docs/architecture/next-steps.md); do not retry ContextStream in the same turn.
- **Code/search:** Call **project(action=index_status)** before the **first** broad code search in a session (or after clone/major changes); if not indexed or stale, run **project(action=ingest_local)** then proceed. Before Grep/Read for code or docs, use **search** (mode=hybrid or semantic). Prefer **search** output_format=paths for file discovery, output_format=count for "how many" or existence checks; use full only when content is needed. Fall back to local tools only if ContextStream returns no results.
- **Decisions:** Recall with session/memory tools for "why did we…"; after significant decisions, capture with **session(action=capture, event_type=decision, ...)** and include **file path** or **code_refs** in content so the knowledge graph links the decision to the doc/module. See [development guide](../../docs/guides/development.md#ai-tooling-optional).
- **Graph:** Before refactors, use **graph(action=dependencies, ...)** and **graph(action=impact, target=...)**. Ensure repo is indexed (see Code/search). After clone or major doc/code changes, run **project(action=ingest_local)** once. Optionally **graph(action=ingest)** for full graph (Elite/Team).
- **New workspace / empty memory:** If this is a new workspace or memory seems empty, run the one-time bootstrap (init + capture key decisions from ADRs/AGENTS.md) as in the [development guide](../../docs/guides/development.md#optional-one-time-bootstrap).
- **Lessons:** When the user corrects a mistake or says "don't do X again", use **session(action=capture_lesson, ...)** with trigger, impact, prevention, keywords.
- **Tagging:** Repo docs use stable IDs (PRD-XXX, ADR-XXX, TP-XXX) and **Related** / **Implements**. See [ContextStream mapping](../../docs/guides/contextstream-mapping.md). **PR ↔ Tech Plan ↔ PRD:** Every PR must use the PR template with **Traceability** (TP-XXX, PRD-XXX), **Doc links** (links to PRD/TP docs per [.github/traceability-mapping.yaml](../../.github/traceability-mapping.yaml)), and **traceability labels** from [.github/labels.yaml](../../.github/labels.yaml). When capturing an **implementation** event, use the traceability mapping to set **code_refs** to the TP and PRD file paths (see [§1.4](../../docs/guides/contextstream-mapping.md#14-linking-pull-requests-to-tech-plans-and-prds-graph-visible)).
- **Router / progressive mode:** If ContextStream is configured with Router or progressive mode (e.g. CONTEXTSTREAM_PROGRESSIVE_MODE), fewer tools may be exposed; use the tools your client lists.
- **API docs:** Each Worker endpoint is documented in **docs/api/openapi.yaml** and served in Swagger at **/api-docs**. Smoke test ensures API documentation loads. When adding or changing API routes, update the OpenAPI spec and keep endpoints in sync.
- **Before pushing to remote:** Run local tests; **at least 80% of tests must pass** before pushing. See [Run tests before push](../../docs/guides/development.md#run-tests-before-push). Block or warn on push if the threshold is not met.

Do not duplicate [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) stack or phase here; ContextStream complements it with persistent memory and code intelligence.
